WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.110
A Node.js application's attack surface begins where untrusted data crosses into trusted

00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:06.060
application logic.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:10.540
Request handlers, routes, controllers, middleware, body parsers, file upload handlers,

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:13.000
cookies, headers, query strings, route parameters,

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.000
and API payloads all shape what the application believes about the outside world.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.885
Each boundary deserves an explicit decision about validation, authorization,

00:00:20.885 --> 00:00:24.000
and error handling. The runtime surface is broader than HTTP.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Environment variables may contain secrets, feature flags, URLs,

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:28.995
and deployment-specific behavior.

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:33.870
File system access can expose paths, temporary files, uploads, generated reports,

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:35.000
and configuration.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.165
Child processes can turn a small input-handling mistake into a system-level risk if

00:00:39.165 --> 00:00:41.000
command construction is unsafe.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Network calls can expose internal services when outbound requests are not controlled.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.235
Data stores and third-party integrations also extend the surface.

00:00:48.235 --> 00:00:53.010
Database queries, object storage, queues, caches, background jobs, webhooks, payment APIs,

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:54.185
identity providers,

00:00:54.185 --> 00:00:58.980
and notification systems all receive or produce data that may affect security decisions.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:03.365
A background job may run outside the normal request path but still process user-controlled

00:01:03.365 --> 00:01:03.980
content.

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:08.000
Logs may look passive, yet they can expose sensitive information if treated casually.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:13.300
A useful mental model is to trace every path from input to effect. Where does data enter?

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:18.000
What transforms it? What policy checks happen? What service receives it? What is logged?

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.000
What happens on failure? This view keeps the conversation grounded.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.000
Security is not only about one route or one library.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.000
It is about how trust moves through the whole Node.js service.
